WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.246
Western Ukraine...

00:00:01.246 --> 00:00:06.040
So I've heard of it since pretty much
day one in this country, in Ukraine.

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:07.054
Everyone says

00:00:07.054 --> 00:00:11.265
"Western Ukraine, Western Ukraine,
you have to see this part of the country."

00:00:11.265 --> 00:00:14.011
So finally... Finally...

00:00:14.011 --> 00:00:15.211
♪ upbeat jazz ♪

00:00:22.216 --> 00:00:23.226
[splash]

00:00:25.583 --> 00:00:26.623
[music fades]

00:00:27.317 --> 00:00:29.384
Getting into Ivano-Frankivsk...

00:00:30.261 --> 00:00:31.860
First impressions...

00:00:32.518 --> 00:00:33.964
It felt relaxed.

00:00:33.964 --> 00:00:37.456
It felt sort of like a mellow small city.

00:00:37.456 --> 00:00:38.905
It was Sunday morning.

00:00:38.905 --> 00:00:40.912
Didn't spend too much time there,
we went south

00:00:41.653 --> 00:00:44.732
through these flat lands.

00:00:44.732 --> 00:00:47.426
Felt nice to be in a car and cruising

00:00:47.426 --> 00:00:50.498
and then the hills
started to come into the view.

00:00:50.542 --> 00:00:54.153
The trees started to come up around us

00:00:54.153 --> 00:00:58.457
and it started to feel
really cool being in nature.

00:00:58.776 --> 00:01:00.056
♪ mellow organ ♪

00:01:09.208 --> 00:01:11.408
[church bells and birds chirping]

00:01:12.534 --> 00:01:13.894
[organ continues]

00:01:18.737 --> 00:01:20.257
[horse trotting by]

00:01:21.207 --> 00:01:25.734
One of the first observations
in the Carpathians were all the churches.

00:01:25.734 --> 00:01:27.870
 I don't know for sure
but it seems from the outside...

00:01:27.870 --> 00:01:29.056
It seems more religious.

00:01:29.056 --> 00:01:31.496
It's Greek Catholic.

00:01:31.891 --> 00:01:34.792
So less of the orthodox.

00:01:34.792 --> 00:01:36.169
Ukrainians know this obviously

00:01:36.169 --> 00:01:42.246
but for outsiders
it's like a big shift in the religion.

00:01:43.063 --> 00:01:44.620
♪ Eurodance ♪

00:01:55.414 --> 00:01:57.504
And then got to our first place

00:01:57.504 --> 00:02:02.493
and our first place
was this beautiful house

00:02:02.493 --> 00:02:04.173
that this family owned

00:02:04.542 --> 00:02:05.520
and

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:06.942
we stayed there for a couple days.

00:02:06.942 --> 00:02:09.049
So we did this hike...

00:02:09.935 --> 00:02:11.835
Babe, what was the name of the hike?

00:02:11.835 --> 00:02:12.835
Hoverla?

00:02:13.183 --> 00:02:16.297
Hoverla, the highest peak in Ukraine.

00:02:16.455 --> 00:02:18.135
I heard it's gonna rain.

00:02:19.372 --> 00:02:21.052
So we're prepared with...

00:02:21.406 --> 00:02:22.655
Well, all this.

00:02:22.892 --> 00:02:23.892
[laughing]

00:02:23.892 --> 00:02:27.348
You must be well-trained
hiking in Kyiv every day, right?

00:02:28.166 --> 00:02:29.166
NATALIA: Oh, yeah.

00:02:30.053 --> 00:02:31.853
NATALIA: What have you got?

00:02:32.977 --> 00:02:34.407
Well, the essentials, obviously.

00:02:34.407 --> 00:02:36.607
Chocolate, chocolate, and then...

00:02:37.742 --> 00:02:38.742
Peanuts.

00:02:39.232 --> 00:02:40.965
NATALIA: Very, very salty.

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:43.613
&lt;These are salty peanuts
to eat with the beer.

00:02:43.613 --> 00:02:45.142
We want salt 'cause we're gonna be...

00:02:45.142 --> 00:02:46.986
NATALIA: It's to eat with the beer, babe.
[giggles]

00:02:46.986 --> 00:02:49.191
No beer, okay, let's go.

00:02:49.616 --> 00:02:51.296
♪ upbeat electronic ♪

00:02:55.293 --> 00:02:57.093
But you know what she said?

00:02:57.626 --> 00:02:59.222
Don't go there.

00:02:59.575 --> 00:03:03.715
Green is bad right now because
it's very slippery after the rain.

00:03:03.715 --> 00:03:06.515
So we need to take
the most difficult path.

00:03:06.845 --> 00:03:07.845
[giggling]

00:03:11.755 --> 00:03:13.035
[stream flowing]

00:03:35.262 --> 00:03:37.120
The rain came in pretty strong.

00:03:37.172 --> 00:03:38.972
[rain splashing on ponchos]

00:03:39.616 --> 00:03:40.816
[water flowing]

00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:50.475
Couldn't see much
but nobody turned around.

00:03:50.475 --> 00:03:51.888
Like, everyone went

00:03:51.888 --> 00:03:57.570
and we saw everyone from a man
with a shopping bag and a cane

00:03:57.570 --> 00:04:00.834
[chuckles] to like a four-year-old
hiking this thing.

00:04:01.568 --> 00:04:04.256
He didn't look happy
but he was hiking it with his parents.

00:04:04.522 --> 00:04:06.358
This is what I love about Ukraine.

00:04:06.358 --> 00:04:07.560
All these students, right...

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:10.176
And they're all hanging out together
and just having a great time.

00:04:11.038 --> 00:04:13.305
MAN: It was hard but we're here.
PETER: Yeah.

00:04:13.305 --> 00:04:14.905
MAN: We're doing it.

00:04:16.155 --> 00:04:17.155
In the rain

00:04:17.836 --> 00:04:19.777
and all these families
were going for the top

00:04:19.777 --> 00:04:23.961
and nobody seemed to mind
that they were getting soaking wet.

00:04:24.601 --> 00:04:26.734
Then at the top it was like a...

00:04:27.388 --> 00:04:29.129
Like a festivity, like a party.

00:04:29.129 --> 00:04:30.512
People had champagne out

00:04:30.512 --> 00:04:34.864
and the number one asset to the country,
in my opinion, is just that...

00:04:35.493 --> 00:04:38.974
How society is so connected together.

00:04:39.927 --> 00:04:42.401
NATALIA: But the way down
is always harder.

00:04:43.317 --> 00:04:44.317
No.

00:04:44.317 --> 00:04:46.417
Gravity... Gravity is helping.

00:04:46.827 --> 00:04:48.347
How was that, babe?

00:04:48.991 --> 00:04:51.458
Eventually it's always cool. [laughs]

00:04:52.131 --> 00:04:53.425
Like when it's done?

00:04:53.425 --> 00:04:54.425
[hands slap]
Yeah, baby.

00:04:54.425 --> 00:04:55.425
Woo.

00:04:56.168 --> 00:04:58.121
I think it was, what? Third day.

00:04:58.121 --> 00:05:00.468
Went south.

00:05:00.673 --> 00:05:03.213
So deeper into the Carpathians.

00:05:03.472 --> 00:05:05.605
I think this is gonna pass over.

00:05:05.832 --> 00:05:08.599
You know, couple minutes,
sun's gonna come out.

00:05:08.599 --> 00:05:10.119
[loud river rapids]

00:05:23.776 --> 00:05:24.776
No comment.

00:05:24.776 --> 00:05:25.896
[truck engine]

00:05:35.633 --> 00:05:38.990
And so it rained, it rained,
and then it rained.

00:05:39.197 --> 00:05:40.997
Then afterwards, it rained.

00:05:42.153 --> 00:05:43.833
It got more beautiful.

00:05:44.078 --> 00:05:46.481
The villages were very nice.

00:05:46.481 --> 00:05:47.841
Like really cute.

00:05:48.585 --> 00:05:50.458
Beautiful villages.

00:05:58.361 --> 00:06:02.183
-How's the Carpathians so far, Nana?
-Cool.

00:06:02.675 --> 00:06:06.036
NATALIA: Cool, wet,
but green and beautiful.

00:06:09.081 --> 00:06:10.081
I concur.

00:06:10.123 --> 00:06:11.350
Oh, check this out.

00:06:11.350 --> 00:06:13.617
We got a little situation up here.

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:16.420
♪ dance music ♪

00:06:27.891 --> 00:06:29.556
Surprisingly for Ukraine

00:06:29.556 --> 00:06:32.335
the roads were actually nice.

00:06:32.479 --> 00:06:35.351
Like really smooth and new

00:06:35.946 --> 00:06:36.946
but then

00:06:37.179 --> 00:06:40.207
the second I said that it changed.

00:06:40.592 --> 00:06:41.952
And... [chuckles]

00:06:42.011 --> 00:06:47.672
It went back to what people typically
think of Ukrainian country side roads as.

00:06:47.825 --> 00:06:49.505
[gravel crunching]

00:06:57.697 --> 00:06:58.977
-Want one?
-Yeah.

00:07:01.250 --> 00:07:02.930
How do the peaches taste?

00:07:03.450 --> 00:07:04.490
NATALIA: Mmm.

00:07:05.088 --> 00:07:06.644
Don't make a porn out of this, love.

00:07:06.644 --> 00:07:08.314
Just tell us how they taste.

00:07:08.613 --> 00:07:12.164
Romanian started coming
over the radio station.

00:07:12.318 --> 00:07:14.938
[woman speaking Romanian on radio]
PETER: Is that Romanian?

00:07:16.217 --> 00:07:17.851
NATALIA: I think that's Italian.

00:07:18.042 --> 00:07:20.442
PETER: Romanian sounds like Italian.

00:07:20.818 --> 00:07:22.565
And Romanian's a beautiful language.

00:07:22.565 --> 00:07:24.245
[woman speaking on radio]

00:07:25.749 --> 00:07:29.306
And this Romanian influence,
you can start to feel it

00:07:29.306 --> 00:07:30.649
as you get closer to the border

00:07:30.649 --> 00:07:33.259
and the people look a bit different

00:07:34.183 --> 00:07:37.127
and it feels like
a different Ukraine actually.

00:07:37.544 --> 00:07:39.381
Look the Carpathians...

00:07:40.243 --> 00:07:44.593
For me, feel like a much different Ukraine
than from what I've seen.

00:07:44.593 --> 00:07:49.053
Like the Far East
where I lived last summer and here...

00:07:49.876 --> 00:07:51.215
Two different worlds.

00:07:51.215 --> 00:07:52.405
I like 'em both

00:07:52.405 --> 00:07:54.849
but completely different.

00:07:55.283 --> 00:07:57.558
Nana is having an existential crisis

00:07:57.558 --> 00:08:00.032
and we haven't been able
to find a pee place

00:08:00.032 --> 00:08:01.354
and this doesn't suffice.

00:08:01.354 --> 00:08:03.288
What about right there, love?

00:08:03.378 --> 00:08:05.361
[Natalia scoffs and giggles]

00:08:05.786 --> 00:08:06.786
No.

00:08:08.140 --> 00:08:09.496
PETER: Do you wish you took a pee

00:08:09.496 --> 00:08:12.696
30 minutes ago at that spot
that we pulled over to?

00:08:14.474 --> 00:08:15.474
Yes.

00:08:16.449 --> 00:08:17.809
[Peter chuckling]

00:08:17.892 --> 00:08:19.572
♪ mellow electronic ♪

00:08:22.596 --> 00:08:25.205
The borders are weird
depending on the countries in the world.

00:08:25.205 --> 00:08:29.058
There's always a lot of
dark sh*t happening.

00:08:29.995 --> 00:08:32.193
And under the surface...

00:08:32.456 --> 00:08:34.256
Like something's getting...

00:08:35.522 --> 00:08:36.522
You know...

00:08:36.645 --> 00:08:40.869
Someone's making a lot of money
doing illegal activity most likely.

00:08:41.189 --> 00:08:42.851
That's the story. Who cares?

00:08:42.851 --> 00:08:44.917
It was just interesting to see...

00:08:45.711 --> 00:08:46.711
[chuckles]

00:08:47.474 --> 00:08:48.695
These mansions...

00:08:49.162 --> 00:08:51.429
And like a lot of them, incomplete

00:08:51.548 --> 00:08:53.376
but there are a lot of big houses.

00:08:53.376 --> 00:08:55.180
And look, this town had nothing.

00:08:55.180 --> 00:08:57.457
There was nothing here
other than a border.

00:08:57.457 --> 00:08:59.137
There wasn't any industry.

00:08:59.473 --> 00:09:01.206
No cities around, nothing.

00:09:01.415 --> 00:09:04.615
And so it was like
big house, big house, big house.

00:09:05.093 --> 00:09:07.093
It was a last minute decision

00:09:08.121 --> 00:09:12.224
to take a left and go park the car

00:09:12.224 --> 00:09:13.904
and walk into Romania.

00:09:14.605 --> 00:09:16.938
In the last bit of the journey here

00:09:17.070 --> 00:09:19.789
on the road trip has felt like
we've been in a different country.

00:09:19.789 --> 00:09:22.122
It hasn't felt like Ukraine at all.

00:09:22.433 --> 00:09:24.113
Walked over the border

00:09:24.715 --> 00:09:28.216
and Romania just felt totally different.

00:09:28.753 --> 00:09:29.753
Like...

00:09:30.391 --> 00:09:32.071
It felt more Italian.

00:09:32.329 --> 00:09:33.530
Some of these...

00:09:33.530 --> 00:09:36.230
The language obviously
and some of the architecture.

00:09:36.230 --> 00:09:37.867
Little bit of the architecture.

00:09:37.867 --> 00:09:39.695
PETER: Doesn't look like much is going on

00:09:39.695 --> 00:09:42.425
in this town we don't know the name of.

00:09:42.928 --> 00:09:45.242
The beauty of road tripping is you just...

00:09:45.816 --> 00:09:47.544
If you leave it open enough you can just

00:09:47.544 --> 00:09:50.144
take on these little adventures like this.

00:09:50.144 --> 00:09:52.759
And we're just gonna be in Romania
for about an hour.

00:09:52.759 --> 00:09:54.808
-My first time, your first time.
-Yeah.

00:09:55.120 --> 00:09:58.769
PETER: And then get back into
the Ukrainian Carpathians.

00:09:58.769 --> 00:10:03.396
Which feel, to me,
much more special than this place.

00:10:03.429 --> 00:10:06.669
So we just cruised around there
for like a couple hours.

00:10:06.669 --> 00:10:08.718
And that was right on the border, right?

00:10:08.718 --> 00:10:10.585
So we cruised away and we got

00:10:11.466 --> 00:10:13.216
to our second place we were gonna stay.

00:10:15.980 --> 00:10:17.690
♪ peaceful piano ♪

00:10:34.323 --> 00:10:35.709
Road inoperable.

00:10:35.894 --> 00:10:39.171
And this guy Vitali
owns this place up the hill.

00:10:39.258 --> 00:10:40.896
He built it with his family.

00:10:40.896 --> 00:10:43.510
It overlooks a valley in the mountains

00:10:43.510 --> 00:10:44.970
and he's an interesting character.

00:10:44.970 --> 00:10:47.599
He's like this super-authentic nature man.

00:10:47.599 --> 00:10:51.117
He runs 30 to 50 kilometers a day.

00:10:51.117 --> 00:10:52.902
Something insane like that.

00:10:52.902 --> 00:10:54.264
Doesn't really sleep.

00:10:54.264 --> 00:10:55.536
I don't think he likes sleep.

00:10:55.536 --> 00:10:57.428
I don't think he really eats much

00:10:57.428 --> 00:11:00.231
but this is like
passion and soul he's put into it

00:11:00.231 --> 00:11:02.708
and that's the thing about money.

00:11:02.708 --> 00:11:04.377
You cannot buy that.

00:11:04.377 --> 00:11:07.870
You can stay at the nicest
five star accommodation

00:11:08.489 --> 00:11:10.169
but you're not gonna get

00:11:10.868 --> 00:11:13.149
that person just giving all he's got.

00:11:13.427 --> 00:11:15.438
Vitali's chai.

00:11:16.105 --> 00:11:17.172
His tea.

00:11:17.172 --> 00:11:18.674
PETER: Special...
VITALI: Black tea.

00:11:18.674 --> 00:11:19.674
[chuckling]

00:11:20.748 --> 00:11:23.309
Special tea from the forest.

00:11:23.442 --> 00:11:25.376
So two places we've stayed at

00:11:26.032 --> 00:11:28.432
people are loving what they're doing

00:11:28.927 --> 00:11:31.291
and they put a lot into it and it shows.

00:11:31.291 --> 00:11:32.786
Yesterday he took us on this hike.

00:11:32.786 --> 00:11:33.786
♪ peaceful piano ♪

00:11:33.786 --> 00:11:36.386
Beautiful hike overlooking the valleys.

00:11:36.495 --> 00:11:39.377
It's not these mind blowing peaks.

00:11:39.672 --> 00:11:40.672
It's not...

00:11:41.684 --> 00:11:44.962
It's not the Himalaya or the Kackars

00:11:45.672 --> 00:11:46.672
or the Alps

00:11:47.679 --> 00:11:48.914
but it's a special place.

00:11:48.914 --> 00:11:50.914
It's got a lot of depth to it.

00:11:51.117 --> 00:11:53.651
A lot of people living for the summer

00:11:54.091 --> 00:11:56.625
picking blueberries
and these little red berries.

00:11:56.625 --> 00:11:58.759
I don't even know what they are.

00:11:59.839 --> 00:12:01.359
[music intensifies]

00:12:29.512 --> 00:12:30.552
[music fades]

00:12:31.571 --> 00:12:33.304
♪ upbeat Ukrainian dance ♪

00:12:47.366 --> 00:12:50.021
Word has it Vitali's got some new shoes

00:12:50.021 --> 00:12:53.456
here at Noha Posta.

00:12:58.284 --> 00:12:59.564
Very good brand.

00:13:03.105 --> 00:13:04.105
PETER: Oh.

00:13:09.341 --> 00:13:13.035
So Vitali gets these shoes
for free from Scarpa

00:13:13.035 --> 00:13:15.447
because he's such a bad*ss on the trails.

00:13:29.939 --> 00:13:32.006
[leaves rustling and footsteps]

00:13:32.050 --> 00:13:33.490
VITALI: Good work.

00:13:44.611 --> 00:13:45.735
NATALIA: He will miss us.

00:13:45.735 --> 00:13:47.256
PETER: That's what this country offers.

00:13:47.256 --> 00:13:48.324
That's what it really...

00:13:48.324 --> 00:13:49.435
The true...

00:13:50.029 --> 00:13:51.495
The true asset

00:13:52.198 --> 00:13:53.198
of here

00:13:53.905 --> 00:13:55.265
underneath it all

00:13:55.783 --> 00:13:56.783
no matter

00:13:57.288 --> 00:13:58.979
what the surface is like.

00:13:58.979 --> 00:14:00.339
There's like this...

00:14:00.805 --> 00:14:01.921
This depth.

00:14:02.407 --> 00:14:04.940
And I get it, there's a dark side too

00:14:05.283 --> 00:14:06.894
but there's a very light

00:14:07.667 --> 00:14:09.530
human, beautiful side to it.

00:14:10.495 --> 00:14:11.899
That's nice to connect into.

00:14:12.085 --> 00:14:13.218
♪ peaceful piano ♪

00:14:13.218 --> 00:14:14.218
[claps]

00:14:14.710 --> 00:14:16.070
That's the story.

00:14:17.085 --> 00:14:20.107
And I'll have to come back
and do some more

00:14:20.107 --> 00:14:22.064
because that was just...

00:14:22.442 --> 00:14:23.442
A scratch...

00:14:24.055 --> 00:14:25.134
On the surface.

00:14:25.809 --> 00:14:26.809
Okay.

00:14:27.170 --> 00:14:28.450
To be continued.

